; 39-hint.kurt

; `hint` is a toggle (`hint on` / `hint off`) for the interactive shell: with
; `hint on`, Kurt prints before each prompt what could come next, e.g.
;
;     ; hint: next, e.g. proof  (Tab writes it)
;
; -- `proof` after a `show`, in a proof its goal and then `qed`, in a chain
; its relation, in a `case` block the other alternatives of the disjunction.
; Tab on an empty line writes it. In a file, `hint` changes nothing.

hint                ; reports the current setting ("hint off")
hint on
hint                ; ("hint on")
hint off
